Where upstream's v0.39 text names a macOS behavior this build has otherwise, it says what ngterm does: the row tints'
AppKit system colors are the same on Linux and Windows, their dark variant on a dark sidebar
(`crates/ngterm-gpui/src/sidebar/look.rs`); the browser override chord for a link is ctrl+shift-click on Linux and
Windows (`ngterm_core::link_policy::wants_browser`); New Companion and Duplicate as Companion sit in the File menu, as
upstream's own menus have them (`crates/ngterm-gpui/src/app_menu.rs`); a Windows machine cannot be the far side of a
remote attach or a remote companion, since every remote call is a POSIX `/bin/sh -c` line
(`crates/ngterm-core/src/remote/tree.rs`, `remote_cli_chain`). Upstream's #821 correction, that links need ⌘⇧ even
with `mouse-reporting = false`, holds for libghostty's own link detection only: this build finds links itself and
follows that setting (`crates/ngterm-gpui/src/terminal/mouse.rs`), so the text keeps "always-on selection and links".
Applied after 0008-show-image-windows.patch.

